    ],
    "details": "In `GCCBootstrap_jll` `9.4.0+0`, the affected target artifacts ship Binutils 2.38: `aarch64-linux-musl`, `armv6l-linux-gnueabihf`, `armv6l-linux-musleabihf`, `armv7l-linux-gnueabihf`, `armv7l-linux-musleabihf`, `i686-linux-gnu`, `i686-linux-musl`, `i686-w64-mingw32`, `powerpc64le-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-linux-musl`, `x86_64-w64-mingw32`. The `aarch64-linux-gnu` target artifact ships Binutils 2.29.1 and is outside the reported affected upstream range.\n\nAn illegal memory access flaw was found in the binutils package. Parsing an ELF file containing corrupt symbol version information may result in a denial of service. This issue is the result of an incomplete fix for CVE-2020-16599.",
